1
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:18,000
What if you had a second chance with the one that got away?

2
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:30,000
Before Sunset is a drama, romance film directed by Richard Linklater.

3
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Nine years later, Jesse travels across Europe giving readings from a book
he wrote about the night he spent in Vienna with Celine.

4
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:54,000
After his reading in Paris, Celine finds him, and they spend part of the
day together before Jesse has to again leave for a flight.

5
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
They are both in relationships now, and Jesse has a son, but as their strong
feelings for each other start to return, both confess a longing for more.

6
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Jesse, played by Ethan Hawke.

7
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Céline, played by Julie Delpy.

8
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:42,000
Bookstore Manager, played by Vernon Dobtcheff.

9
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Journalist #1, played by Louise Lemoine Torrès.

10
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Journalist #2, played by Rodolphe Pauly.

11
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Waitress, played by Mariane Plasteig.

12
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Before Sunset is a 2004 American romantic drama film directed by Richard Linklater, who co-wrote the
screenplay with Ethan Hawke and Julie Delpy, from a story by Linklater and Kim Krizan.

13
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:42,000
It is the first film by Warner Independent Pictures.

14
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:54,000
The sequel to Before Sunrise (1995) and the second installment in the Before trilogy, Before Sunset
follows Jesse (Hawke) and Céline (Delpy) as they reunite nine years later in Paris.

15
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Linklater, Krizan, Hawke, and Delpy began developing a larger budget sequel in
the 1990s, but failed to secure funding to begin production.

16
00:51:12,000 --> 00:51:18,000
After writing the film independently, with portions inspired by Hawke's separation (and eventual divorce) from Uma Thurman, the writers came together in 2003 and
incorporated elements of their individual screenplays, as well as other scenes written during development of Before Sunrise, to create the final screenplay.

17
00:54:24,000 --> 00:54:30,000
Principal photography took place entirely in Paris, and the
film is considered to take place in real time.

18
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:42,000
Delpy also contributed original music to the film's soundtrack.

19
01:00:48,000 --> 01:00:54,000
Before Sunset premiered at the Berlin International Film Festival on February 10,
2004; it was theatrically released in the United States on July 2, 2004.

20
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
It grossed $15 million worldwide and received widespread critical acclaim, particularly for
Linklater's direction, the performances and chemistry of its leads, and its screenplay.

21
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
It received numerous accolades, being nominated for the Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay, and appeared on many
publications' lists of the best films of the year, with some calling it one of the best of the decade.

22
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:30,000
It was followed by a third film, Before Midnight, in 2013.

23
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:42,000
The film explores themes of journalist, talking,
soulmates, walking, paris, france.

24
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:54,000
The tone is emotional.
